Z||000005||Black88GT||09-07-2000||10:38 PM||||go to <A HREF="http://www.subarusvx.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subarusvx.com</A> <P>I went there and found out some cool stuff.  Not all of them were AWD.  They had all aluminum DOHC 3.3 V6s.  Not that fast and I heard parts were really hard to find and expensive since they were so rare.  I remember the last year they made them, '97, they only sold 1,111.  I liked them a lot though, my friend had one for a while until he wrecked it.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||14
Z||000006||HYPTNOTiSE||09-09-2000||08:04 AM||||Holy crap standard!  I was just about to start this thread.  I'm think of getting one, pretty serious actually. The years to get are 94.5-97, but you'll pay highly for a 97.  I'm looking for a black 95LSi or but blue, white, or polo green is cool too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  These cars aren't quick, but they're fast.  0-60 in 7.5-8.0 sec and only available with automatic.  But i talked to a guy last night that has no problem going 140mph in stock form.  I think they're really cool cars. But had tranny problems the first few years, so check on that. They make 233hp at the crank(which is forged by the way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  They put 170hp to all 4 wheels.  Very cool looking cars. <A HREF="http://www.siue.edu/~efrankl/svx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.siue.edu/~efrankl/svx.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.cars101.com/subaru_svx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cars101.com/subaru_svx.html</A> <BR>Those are my to fav sites.<BR><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
